{\underline{\it Decoding Rule 2}:} In contrast, the second decoding rule makes use of the tests that do not include the item. More precisely, let ${{s}_{i}}$ denote the number of tests that item $i$ is excluded from, and let ${{s}_{i}^+}$ (respectively ${{s}_{i}^-}$) denote the number of tests with positive (respectively negative) outcome within these ${{s}_{i}}$ tests. We then classify $i$ as follows:
