    \right.
\end{equation}
For such $f(\cdot)$, one can see that ${H(f)}\in {\cal O} \left(d^w\right)$, for instance by choosing ${L} = \left \lfloor \frac{d^w}{3} \right \rfloor$ and ${U} = \left \lceil \frac{2d^w}{3} \right \rceil$.

