    &\ge \frac{13}{6} {m} \notag \\ 
    &= 2{m} + \frac{1}{6} \times \frac{12{P_{\min}({q})}}{({\Delta({q})})^2} \ln \left( \frac{2n}{\varepsilon} \right) \notag\\
    &\ge 2{m} + 2\ln \left( \frac{2n}{\varepsilon} \right), \end{align}
where the third line follows from the definition of ${m}$ in \eqref{eq:def:m}; the last line follows from \eqref{eq:1>=pmin>max:Delta}. 

Let $\mathcal{E}_i$ be the event that item $i$ participates in less than ${m}$ tests. By Fact~\ref{chernoff_bound}, we have
\begin{equation*}
