From \eqref{eq:def:fTp}, we know that the value of ${\hat{\Gamma}} ({q})$ depends on the choice of ${q}$. 

For ${q}\in \left(\frac 1 d , \frac {d-1}{d}\right)$ with $d\geq 3$, the following result asserts that by choosing ${q}$ properly, we can give an explicit bound on the value of ${\hat{\Gamma}} ({q})$.





\begin{proposition} Let $d\geq 3$. For any ${L}',{U}' \in \{1 ,\dots, d-1\}$ with ${L}' < {U}'$ and $f({L}')<f({U}')$, there exists ${q}_0 \in \left(\frac {{L}'} {d}, \frac {{U}'} {d}\right)$ such that ${\hat{\Gamma}} ({q}_0)$ in \eqref{eq:def:fTp} satisfies

\begin{equation} {\hat{\Gamma}} ({q}_0) \leq  31334.75 \times \frac{1}{{\alpha}^2} \left( \frac{{U}'-{L}'}{f({U}')-f({L}')} \right)^2  d\log \left( \frac{2n}{\varepsilon } \right)
\end{equation} 
where ${\alpha} := \frac{1}{2} \min\left\{{U}'-{L}',\sqrt{{L}'},\sqrt{d-{U}'}\right\}$.
\end{proposition}
