for some ${q}_0 \in \left( \frac{{L}}{d} , \frac{{U}}{d} \right)$. 
\end{itemize}




Case \ref{unify:item4}: For $0 = {L} < {U} = d$, we have ${\beta}=1$ by definition \eqref{eq:def:beta}. The proof is similar to Case \ref{unify:item2}. Consider three sub-cases:
\begin{itemize}
\item \underline{$d= 1$}: In this sub-case, the two bounds in Proposition \ref{prop:existence_margin} are identical and give 
    \begin{align}
