\end{align}
for some ${q}_0 \in \left( \frac{{L}}{d} , \frac{{U}}{d} \right)$.

Summarizing the above, we see that for any $0\leq {L}<{U}\leq d$, there exists ${q}_0 \in \left( \frac{{L}}{d} , \frac{{U}}{d} \right)$ such that
